## Static findings and checks

- The helper still invokes the exact real compiler driver `/usr/bin/cc`. Redirection requires exactly one separate `-o` argument and an exact match to either `/workspace/.cache/zed/target/debug/deps/koda-145bb81fa8b08935` or the new owned probe output. Other invocations forward their entire `OsString` argument vector unchanged. A selected invocation changes only that output argument; input files and all other flags remain unchanged. The app receipt label and runner glob both use `koda-tree-adapter`.
- `symlink_metadata` refuses any existing original output, including a dangling symlink, and any existing PID-specific redirected output. Receipts use `create_new`. A failed real link preserves a nonzero status and removes its owned incomplete output; helper I/O or publication failures also return nonzero. Successful linking requires a regular-file target before publishing the original output symlink.
- The app command remains exactly `cargo build --locked -p zed --bin koda`. The retry runner verifies the supplied lowercase 40-hex commit against HEAD. It hashes all four crate roots, changes only their mtimes, verifies their bytes immediately afterward, and rechecks them after Cargo. A nonzero Cargo result is recorded and propagated before ELF-success assertions.
- Successful-build assertions still require exactly one final-link receipt, one argv difference immediately after `-o`, a zero real-link status, original and Cargo top-level paths resolving to the redirected executable, and an ELF header. The executable's size and SHA are recorded only after those assertions. These are prepared checks, not evidence that a build has occurred.
- The whole-source guard keeps the prior HEAD, index, worktree, and untracked-file checks and before/after hashes. Its `PATHS` value was independently parsed and compared exactly with the fixed exclusions: direct `docs/android-studio/*.md`, `reference-manifest.json`, `test-parity.json`, direct `ports/*.json`, and evidence `**/*.log` / `**/*.json`. Source, dependencies, fixtures, Cargo files, assets, PNG/SVG files, and nested port data receive no added exclusion. Both Python files parse successfully without being executed.
- The outer runner passes through the child build result. Its post-build Git and byte guards run even when the child returns nonzero; a guard failure also exits unsuccessfully. Raw build output and exit records remain separate, and the scripts do not skip tests, change source, weaken compilation flags, or normalize raw logs.

